      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we document the memory-type contract here? `CLIB_DMA_*` applies to coherent, cacheable DMA memory and only orders accesses—it does not clean caches, force write-through, or make non-coherent DMA buffers visible. Conversely, `CLIB_MMIO_WMB()` orders prior normal-memory stores before a following device-register (MMIO) write; MMIO is device/uncached memory whose accesses can have side effects. This distinction is important so future callers do not use these barriers as a cache-maintenance substitute.",
      "revId": "95bedf569613526b72e41e9f3ce466e9d083cbac",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    }
